<!-- v3 (2026-11-17, help overhaul step 4): written from the v2 screen and
     code, John's structure and the shared blocks in ui/css/help.css. -->
<p>Every artist has a story. Bio Builder writes a short biography for each artist in your library and finds their portrait, for the Library Viewer to show.</p>

<h3>What it does:</h3>
<p>Bio Builder searches the web and has the AI write a biography from what it finds. It also looks for the artist's photo on Discogs. You read it, edit it and save it.</p>

<section class="steps">
    <h3>How to use this tool:</h3>
    <ol>
        <li>Type the artist's name in <strong>Artist</strong> and choose <span class="ui-button">Search</span> (or press Enter). If more than one artist matches, choose the right one.
            <p class="note">Coming from the Dashboard, Database Tools or Album Personnel, the artist is already chosen.</p>
        </li>
        <li>Choose the length: leave <strong>Enhanced bio</strong> off for about 250 to 300 words in three paragraphs, or turn it on for about 450 to 500 words in five.</li>
        <li>Choose <span class="ui-button">Get Biography</span>. The text appears in <strong>Biography</strong>, with a portrait if Discogs has one.</li>
        <li>Read it and edit anything that's wrong. <strong>Sources</strong> lists the web pages it was written from.</li>
        <li>Don't like the portrait? Choose <span class="ui-button">Browse</span> under <strong>Use a portrait from a file</strong> to use your own.</li>
        <li>Choose <span class="ui-button">Save Biography</span>.</li>
    </ol>
    <p class="note">Nothing is saved until you choose Save Biography: not the text, and not the portrait.</p>
</section>

<h3>When there are no sources</h3>
<p>If the web search finds nothing, the AI writes from its own knowledge, and a warning says so. Check the facts carefully before you save.</p>

<h3>Getting a new biography</h3>
<p>Choosing <span class="ui-button">Get Biography</span> again replaces what's in the editor. If there's text in it already, MetaForge asks first: <span class="ui-button">Replace</span> or <span class="ui-button">Keep my text</span>. The saved biography doesn't change until you save.</p>

<h3>Portraits</h3>
<p>Portraits are saved as 500 × 500 pictures in the <code>photos</code> folder inside MetaForge's own folder. A photo that isn't square gets black bands to fill the square, so nothing is cut off.</p>

<p>See also: <button type="button" class="see-also" data-mf-help="personnel" data-mf-help-name="Album Personnel">Album Personnel</button>; <button type="button" class="see-also" data-mf-help="database_tools" data-mf-help-name="Database Tools">Database Tools</button>.</p>
